# Repo only files at this package root, kept out of the home directory. The generated
# manifest, the module level declaration, and the collector with the reader beside it are the
# module's contract with the layer above, so they belong to the repository rather than to the
# running config, and check-timers is a check on the source the running config has no use for.
# grants-probe is the same kind of thing, the module's answer to a question only the layer above
# asks, which happens to work by asking the running config rather than by reading a file.
#
# Nothing inside .hammerspoon is listed. It used to hold declaration files that both the running
# config and the collector read, so they had to be stowed. A plugin declares in its own
# manifest.lua now, which the running config reads as part of the plugin itself, so there is no
# longer a repository only file down there to keep out.
DEPENDENCIES
dependencies-module
dependencies-collect
dependencies-collect.lua
grants-probe
check-timers
# theme-exempt is this package's word to src/check-theme.sh that its chrome is not painted
# from the palette yet, and why.
theme-exempt
